These are beta test versions of CicleMUD 3.0.  Latest patchlevel is 19,
released on August 14, 2001.  Older betas are in the Old-Betas directory.
If you just need an individual file, look in the 'uncompressed' directory.

circle30bpl19.tar.gz, circle30bpl19.bz2, circle30bpl19.zip are all the
same distribution and have the same contents but are compressed
differently.  It is a source distribution that compiles under UNIX,
Windows 95/98/NT, the Amiga, OS/2, Acorn RiscOS, and the Macintosh.
There is information on how to compile under each of these platforms
inside the archive.  There are no binaries provided.

Note that while this is officially still beta-test software, it is a
very ripe beta and is much easier to use than version 2.20, so you can
go ahead and use 3.0 with the understanding that you'll probably have
to patch it a few times as new patchlevels are released.

There are a number of patch files here to bring your release of Circle
up to the current relase (patch.plX-plY will upgrade Circle from
patchlevel X to patchlevel Y).  Use the GNU 'patch' program to apply
the patches.  See the documentation for 'patch' for more information.

-- Jeremy Elson (jelson@circlemud.org)
